WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
Michael Myers.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.629
You can shoot him 6 times, you can even make
6 terrible sequels.

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:07.540
But Michael Myers will never die.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.680
Halloween is back.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.389
Intro.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:14.710
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.950
Today we’re taking a look at the trailer
for Halloween.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.570
I’m gonna be breaking it down shot by shot
for you and pulling out all those juicy Things

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.570
You Missed.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.890
Now when you watch the trailer you’ll notice
something very early on.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.950
Check out this clip.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:32.679
“We’re here to investigate a patient who
killed three innocent teenagers on Halloween

00:00:32.679 --> 00:00:33.780
in 1978.”

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.940
Anyone who’s seen the movies knows he’s
killed a bit more than three people.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.150
I mean probably only our boy Dead Meat knows
the actual number, but what’s going on right

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.150
here?

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.150
What’s the deal with that?

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.700
Well, it was previously believed that this
movie takes place in a fourth or depending

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.190
on your view, possibly fifth alternate universe,
and that it would branch off from the main

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.409
timeline after Halloween 2.

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:56.079
However this trailer claims that after being
shot by Dr. Loomis in the original movie,

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:59.780
Michael was captured and taken into captivity,
where he spent the last 40 years.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.089
That means this takes place in a timeline
where none of these movies happened.

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:05.870
So this is essentially a fresh slate for the
franchise.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.190
That’s not to say it doesn’t have some
homages to those other films hidden in the

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.030
trailer though, so make sure you watch this
whole video to see all of those.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.000
Unfortunately for us, that new timeline means
we may have to sit through yet another scene

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.480
of the characters finding out that Michael
Myers is invincible, as we have painstakingly

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.470
had to do in pretty much every movie.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.450
That’s essentially confirmed when we see
the older Laurie Strode doing target practice

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.560
in her backyard.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.550
And trying to stab him with a knife.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.550
Come on Laurie!

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:32.850
You know better than this!

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.910
Notice the guy at the beginning says that
Michael killed three innocent teenagers (I

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.950
mean are there really such thing as innocent
teenagers though?), but he makes no mention

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.140
of Michael M killing his sister at the age
of 6, which is what happens in the first scene

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.580
of the original 1978 Halloween.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.480
In this movie, Laurie has a granddaughter,
and she has a line that confirms that Michael

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.850
is not even related to her.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.850
“No.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.740
He is not her brother, that is something that
people made up.”

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.340
So that might lead some people to believe
that the opening scene didn’t happen in

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.200
this timeline, but I think they’ve just
neglected to mention the murder of Michael’s

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.480
older sister Judith, because we do still he
a sketch of Dr. Loomis in the police report,

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.890
and it’s mentioned that Michael was shot
by his own psychiatrist.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:15.209
I can’t imagine why he’d have a psychiatrist
without those events taking place in 1963

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:16.209
first.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:20.939
It’s also really the only explanation as
to why do these kids in 2018, 40 years after

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:25.489
the fact, know about a murderer who only killed
three people all those years ago.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:27.620
And to the point that he’s a household name.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.019
And one more thing on the whole idea of Laurie
and Michael not actually being siblings.

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:34.870
My theory is that they’re taking the Halloween
3 approach, to where it takes place in a different

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.760
universe entirely, but the other movies still
exist as fictional movies in this universe.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.510
So in this universe, someone made a “based
on a true story” movie or book about the

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.310
killer Michael Myers, and then sequels started
to come out that were not so based on a true

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.310
story.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.760
That’s where the idea that Laurie and Michael
are siblings may have originated.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.769
Of course, it’s also possible that they
really are related and Laurie just doesn’t

00:02:56.769 --> 00:02:59.560
know it, much like in Rob Zombie’s Halloween
II.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.370
Here we get to see the police reports from
that Halloween night all those years ago,

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.170
and they do contain some nuggets I thought
you might be interested in.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.500
This is Laurie’s injury report, detailing
the slash across right neck and shoulder and

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.750
bruising and contusions around neck.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.219
This is only on screen for less than 1/10th
of a second, but there’s a photograph of

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:20.590
someone’s hand, and this almost looks like
a reflection of the mask, but I might just

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.730
be reading too much into it.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.519
Here we’ve got the large knife, evidence
from the upstairs bedroom, which of course

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:27.400
was labeled with the date 10/31/78.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.769
Then again, only a tenth of a second, they
show off evidence photos of the mask in what

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:32.769
seems to be a tiled room of some kind.

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:34.900
This photo was probably taken after the fact
because it looks like nobody’s wearing the

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.859
mask and the background here is some kind
of tiled area; whereas at the end of Halloween,

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:40.999
Michael ends up in the grass outside the house.

00:03:40.999 --> 00:03:44.760
This is most likely a photo of Tommy Doyle,
the boy that Laurie was babysitting on that

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.760
fateful night.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.560
But behind that we get a little glimpse of
the police report text.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.819
The only interesting thing I pulled from that
is the mention of this “Deputy Miller”,

00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:55.700
who as far as I know, isn’t an existing
character in this franchise, so this may be

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.549
someone new who is retconned into the story.

00:03:58.549 --> 00:04:02.250
Other than that, it just seems to be a recount
of the events of the OG Halloween.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.250
Another question.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:06.390
Who are these people investigating Michael
Myers, and why now?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.950
Why are they trying to get a rise of out of
him by showing the mask?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.370
OK, I guess that’s more than one question.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:15.389
But I think this guy could be disciple of
Dr. Loomis, or in any event, the successor

00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:19.199
to Dr. Loomis who goes into town and warns
people about how dangerous Michael is, just

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:21.250
as Loomis did in the films that he was in.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.110
Unlike his predecessor however, he doesn’t
seem to have given up on his patient just

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.110
yet.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.580
Laurie asks him if he believes in the boogeyman,
and he says no, suggesting he might not see

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.280
Michael as a monster like Laurie does.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.009
The woman that he’s working with is documenting
everything using the audio recorder, and her

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.430
name tag also gives us a couple clues.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.990
First, we see the name of the facility Smith’s
Grove State Hospital.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.009
The original facility that Michael broke out
of in Halloween was called Smith’s Grove

00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:49.300
Sanitarium, so it’s likely the same place
that just got a name at some point along the

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.300
line.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.891
You have to believe if he can break out once
he can do it again.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.050
The chick’s name is Dana Haines.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:58.240
There is a security guard named Haines at
a different hospital known as Grace Anderson

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.930
Sanitarium in Halloween: Resurrection, but
I doubt that’s even a reference seeing as

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:07.300
how hated that movie is, it’s just my job
to point it out to you though.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.639
Wait, hold up, hold up.

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:09.639
OK.

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:10.639
This kid’s a ninja.

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:11.750
This kid’s a skeleton.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.890
What’s this kid supposed to be, Busta Rhymes?

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.360
But on a more serious note, this scene is
a major throwback to the original Halloween

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.389
where Laurie walks home from school with her
two friends, but this time it’s Laurie’s

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:23.389
granddaughter.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.650
They just put this Boba Tea in the shot so
you can tell that this is the 2018 one.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:31.040
Laurie is absolutely crazy in this movie,
she’s basically spent the last 40 years

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.889
preparing for Michael, and if you read between
the lines you can see everyone’s subtle

00:05:34.889 --> 00:05:36.889
condescending behaviour towards her.

00:05:36.889 --> 00:05:40.440
Even her own family treats her like a nutcase.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.440
“Mom?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.440
What bus crashed?”

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.319
Additionally the neighborhood kids seem to
have no respect for her authority.

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:49.580
She’s basically turned her house into a
fortress with cameras, sirens, even a secret

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.580
bunker.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.879
It looks like they’re setting up a classic
old lady who cried wolf scenario.

00:05:53.879 --> 00:05:58.009
Laurie’s been freaking out for the last
40 years over the return of Michael Myers…

00:05:58.009 --> 00:06:03.400
no, not that Return of Michael Myers… and
basically when he does really come back, nobody’s

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.400
gonna take her seriously.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.400
Cause she’s the crazy lady.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.000
This bathroom scene may be a reference to
the opening scene of H20, where a woman is

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.319
attacked by Michael in a rest stop bathroom.

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:14.180
In this case it’s a gas station bathroom,
and it looks like a mechanic also faces the

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.580
wrath of Michael Myers.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.919
So it looks as if a lot of the deaths in this
movie will be callbacks to other moments in

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:22.270
the franchise, despite them not being on this
timeline.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.410
And back to the bathroom stall for a moment,
this drawing on the stall door really stands

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.410
out.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.879
To me it looks like a dog wearing sunglasses
looking to the left, but I couldn’t help

00:06:29.879 --> 00:06:33.940
but notice if you erase part of it, you’ve
got the Cult of Thorn symbol from Halloween

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.990
4, 5, and 6.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.300
Now, do I think the cult will be making an
appearance in this movie?

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.760
No, absolutely not.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.250
It would just be a fun easter egg for the
fans of those movies.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.849
Let me know your interpretation of the bathroom
stall drawing in the comments though.

00:06:47.849 --> 00:06:49.580
I already found my most *DISLIKED* character.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.350
The lady wearing a Christmas sweater on Halloween.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:57.479
A lot of people were confused about this scene,
where Laurie shoots because she thinks she

00:06:57.479 --> 00:06:59.290
sees Michael in the window of this house.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:03.170
Some were comparing it to H20, where Laurie
has constant hallucinations of Michael, but

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.190
if you slow it down it looks like it’s actually
just a mirror that she sees him through.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:11.069
One thing that I found creepy is that there’s
actually somebody in the other room over here,

00:07:11.069 --> 00:07:14.699
watching this all go down, and the person’s
head immediately snaps toward the room that

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:15.699
Michael is in.

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:19.699
Judging by the lighting, I’d say that room
with the blue light is... this room, where

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:23.439
there is yet another reference; this time
to the ghost scene from the first Halloween,

00:07:23.439 --> 00:07:27.319
where Michael wears the ghost sheet over his
head to trick Laurie’s friend Lynda into

00:07:27.319 --> 00:07:30.389
thinking he was her boyfriend, Bob, in order
to get her guard down.

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:34.419
I do think that Laurie’s granddaughter is
going to be the main protagonist in this movie,

00:07:34.419 --> 00:07:38.150
and it looks like one of her friends is a
babysitter, so don’t be surprised if what

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:42.440
goes down in this movie is very similar to
the events of 40 years ago.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.590
If you enjoyed any of these Things You Missed,
feel free to drop a like on this video.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.860
Let me know if the comments who you think
is crazier.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.020
This Laurie, or the Laurie from the Rob Zombie
Halloween films.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.240
Anyway, if you’re new here, I’m CZ.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.289
I write and narrate my own horror stories
as well.

00:07:56.289 --> 00:07:58.849
I just came out with one called Creepy Clown
School Lockdown 2.

00:07:58.849 --> 00:08:02.300
Don’t worry, you don’t need to see the
first one, so go ahead and give it a listen.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:06.210
OK, last announcement, if you’re going to
VidCon come to my fan meetup on Thursday the

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.770
21st at 5:30PM in Room 211.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:12.710
We’re going to raffle off some merch and
there will be other cool creators there as

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:13.710
well.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.389
OK, with that all out of the way, I think
we’re gonna be talking a lot about this

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:22.240
Halloween movie so make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.229
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:08:26.229 --> 00:08:27.819
Assuming we both survive.

